Subject: [PATCH 23/51] B70-IP-D2: CPU tests (spec gate, split views, writer,
 K4 parity, routing)

tests/v1/core/test_b70_ip_d2.py, no GPU:

1. Spec: flag on, FLASH_ATTN packs int8_per_token_head == TRITON_ATTN
   (blocks 64/832/3264, kv heads 1/2/4); flag off or not XPU: spec unchanged
   and the dtype is rejected; the QSA backend keeps the inline packing.
2. Views: split_layout_views equals the kernel test's reference views over the
   raw page bytes (data_ptr, shape, strides, dtype) on NHD and HND logical
   caches, padded pages and a layer offset; 64-B alignment rules of
   check_int8_kv_cache hold; no byte written. Non-compact layouts, unaligned
   padded pages and head_size 96 are refused. The view cache rebuilds after the
   runner's _k_scale_cache reset and on a new cache.
3. Writer (TRITON_INTERPRET=1 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=): FlashAttentionImpl
   .do_kv_cache_update puts the reference quantization (absmax/127, round half
   away, clamp) at the reference byte positions, skips slot -1 and the padded
   key rows, and leaves every other byte (other slots, page padding) alone.
4. K4 parity: the same tokens in an inline cache and a split cache dequantize
   to bit-identical bf16/fp16 blocks; the forced K4 prefill over the split
   cache equals the stock K4 prefill over the inline cache (bit-exact).
5. Routing (stand-in kernels): q 1, causal q 8, ragged q 3/1/5 and non-causal
   q 8 go to one int8 call; a 40-token chunk and non-causal q 20 go to the
   dequant path (with B70_PTH_FA_PREFILL=0 set); all within 1.5e-2 of an fp32
   reference on the dequantized cache.

Result (CPU, torch 2.14.1+cpu, triton 3.9 interpreter): 23 passed; with the
K3/W1 and H1 suites 29 passed. Without TRITON_INTERPRET the 4 writer cases
skip (19 passed). Mutations (K/V scale views swapped, non-causal rows sent to
the causal route) fail the views/writer and routing tests.
